WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.170
In 2015, a US court approved a
415 million dollar settlement.

2
00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.830
The lawsuit claimed that
four big tech firms had

3
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.400
agreed not to recruit each other's staff,

4
00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.110
holding pay down.

5
00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.510
When workers can't easily switch jobs,

6
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.770
an employer can set the wage.

7
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:20.010
Such a firm may even turn away a worker

8
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.120
who would add more to its
sales than their wage.

9
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.720
Why would it do that?

10
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.460
In this mission, you'll
build the monopsony graph,

11
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.970
step by step.

12
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:32.290
Then you'll pick how many
workers to hire in a graph lab,

13
00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.850
and test your pick.

14
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:37.800
Your mission: find out why a
firm would turn that worker away.
